    <statement><p>Find the vector and parametric equations for the line through the point
<m>P=(5, -4, -5)</m> and the point <m>Q=(8, -8, -10)</m>.</p>
<p>Vector Form: <m>\mathbf r = \langle</m><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/>, <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/>, -5 <m>\rangle + t \langle</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/>, <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/>, -5 <m>\rangle</m></p>
<p>Parametric form (parameter <m>t</m>, and passing through <m>P</m> when <m>t = 0</m>):</p>
<p><m>x = x(t) =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
<p><m>y = y(t) =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0006"/></p>
<p><m>z = z(t) =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0007"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5+t\cdot 3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
